Tsfm.Forecasting.Timestral — Apache-2.0, NOT MIT
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

That package contains software derived from Timestral
(https://github.com/mistralai/timestral), Copyright Mistral AI, licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0.

Changes to the derived work, as required by Apache-2.0 section 4(b):

  - The inference path is translated from Python/PyTorch to C#/TorchSharp: the
    causal per-patch scaler, instance scaling of known-future covariates, patch
    representation, the time/variate transformer with gated attention and
    partial rotary embedding, the monotone quantile head, the attention masks
    and positions, and the forecaster's refine frame, quantile cap, symmetric
    averaging and non-negative clipping.
  - Decoder tokens are built for the horizon patches only; the reference also
    builds, then discards, one for every earlier patch.
  - Symmetric averaging runs the negated input in the same forward pass as the
    original, as further groups, instead of in a second call.
  - The advancing refine frame accumulates per-patch Welford states sequentially
    rather than by a parallel prefix scan; both are float64.
  - A context longer than the trained length is refused rather than truncated.
  - Past-only covariates as a separate role, categorical target encoding and the
    block-by-block continuation beyond one decoded block are not ported.

